  "result": "JWT `exp` field = Unix seconds. `Date.now()` = milliseconds.\n\n**Bug:** `Date.now()` is ~1000x larger than `exp`, so expired tokens always pass.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```js\n// Wrong\nif (Date.now() > decoded.exp) { /* never triggers */ }\n\n// Correct\nif (Date.now() / 1000 > decoded.exp) { /* or: */ }\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > decoded.exp) { }\n```\n\nOr use `Date.now() > decoded.exp * 1000` \u2014 same math, different side.\n\nIf using `jsonwebtoken` library, skip manual check entirely \u2014 `jwt.verify()` handles expiry automatically and throws `TokenExpiredError`.",
